## Session tempo transport (Ableton Link compatible, clean-room) and opendeck-link/1

`src/main/ableton-link/` (wire.ts, node.ts) is an original, clean-room
implementation of the Ableton Link wire protocol (discovery, ghost-time
measurement, shared timeline, start/stop), published under OpenDeck's MIT
licence (D44). It was written only from black-box observation of the
reference LinkHutSilent example's network traffic and from public, non-GPL
descriptions; the full list of sources and their licences is in
`docs/link-cleanroom.md`. It contains **no Ableton code**: the reference
library (GPLv2+ or proprietary) was built and run as an opaque binary in an
isolated directory outside this repository, and its source was not opened,
read, searched or copied. No third-party Link implementation's code was used
either; the `ablink` crate (labelled MIT) was evaluated and rejected for
unverifiable provenance, and the `link-bpm` crate (MIT/Apache-2.0) was used
only for the multicast address stated in its README.

`src/main/link.ts` is the original opendeck-link/1 protocol (D34), kept as the
OpenDecks-only fallback (`239.255.77.88:29876`).

The verification helper `scripts/link-peer-pty.py` drives an externally built
LinkHutSilent through a terminal; neither that binary nor any Ableton code is
distributed with OpenDecks.

"Ableton" and "Link" are trademarks of Ableton AG. They are used here only to
describe protocol compatibility (nominative use). OpenDecks is not affiliated
with, endorsed by or certified by Ableton, and does not use the Link logo or
badge.

