## Reference material

The Serato file-format behaviour implemented by the import/export code was
documented from publicly available community reverse-engineering notes
([serato-tags](https://github.com/Holzhaus/serato-tags), the Mixxx wiki and
[rb2serato](https://github.com/SM4RTENHEIMER/rb2serato), all MIT-licensed
documentation/projects). No source code from those projects is vendored into
OpenDeck; see `docs/interop.md` for the specific claims and links.

### Pro DJ Link, rekordbox export and NFS (references only)

The CDJ / USB-drive import in `src/main/prolink/` is an original, clean-room
implementation written from protocol and file-format descriptions. No source
code from any other implementation was read, copied, ported or linked; in
particular nothing from Beat Link, Crate Digger (EPL), prolink-connect,
python-prodj-link or the Rust `prolink` crates (GPL). References used:

- Deep Symmetry, "DJ Link Ecosystem Analysis" (prose and packet diagrams:
  startup, detailed device status, media slot queries) —
  https://djl-analysis.deepsymmetry.org/djl-analysis/
- Deep Symmetry, "Rekordbox Export Structure Analysis" (export.pdb and ANLZ
  file descriptions) — https://djl-analysis.deepsymmetry.org/rekordbox-export-analysis/
- RFC 1057 (ONC RPC v2), RFC 1014 (XDR), RFC 1094 (NFS v2 and MOUNT v1).

